# Local-dev-only secrets for `wrangler dev` (Cloudflare's convention: a
# .dev.vars file, gitignored, never committed). Copy this to `.dev.vars` and
# fill in real values for local testing only.
#
# In production these are NOT set as files — use:
#   wrangler secret put BOT_TOKEN
#   wrangler secret put WEBHOOK_SECRET
# which stores them encrypted on Cloudflare's side, never in the repo.

# Token from @BotFather. Never commit this, never put it in frontend code.
BOT_TOKEN=

# Any random string you generate yourself (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
# Passed to Telegram's setWebhook as secret_token, and checked against the
# X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token header on every incoming webhook call.
WEBHOOK_SECRET=
